Indices: 012345
$s[0] = \text{W}$
$s[1] = \text{B}$. Not covered. We need an operation.
Greedy choice: Start at index 1. Interval $[1, 3]$. Covers indices 1, 2, 3.
Count = 1. Last covered up to index 3.
$s[2]$ covered.
$s[3]$ covered.
$s[4] = \text{W}$.
$s[5] = \text{B}$. Not covered (since $5 > 3$).
We need an operation. Start at index 5. Interval $[5, 7]$. Covers 5.
Count = 2. Last covered up to index 7.
End of string. Total operations = 2.
